# {{ .Project }} API

Generated with aspgen using Clean Architecture. The dependency direction is:

```text
WebApi -> Infrastructure -> Application -> Domain
```

## Build

Run these commands from the generated project root:

```powershell
dotnet restore .\{{ .Project }}.sln
dotnet build .\{{ .Project }}.sln
```

## Run the API

```powershell
dotnet run --project .\src\WebApi\WebApi.csproj --urls http://localhost:5000
```

Useful endpoints:

- Health: `http://localhost:5000/health`
- OpenAPI: `http://localhost:5000/openapi/v1.json`
- Scalar UI: `http://localhost:5000/scalar/v1`

The default database is SQLite. Its database file is configured in `src/WebApi/appsettings.json`.
For PostgreSQL, generate with `--database postgres` and update the connection string before running.

## Add a feature or entity

```powershell
aspgen add entity Book title:string pages:int published:date --project .
aspgen add feature SearchBooks title:string --project .
```

Run `aspgen new` before any `add` command. Incremental files are registered in their owning project file.
